.TH ED25519 2
.SH NAME
ed25519: verify \- Ed25519 signature verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "sys.m";
include "keyring.m";
include "ed25519.m";
ed25519 := load Ed25519 Ed25519->PATH;

init:   fn(): string;
verify: fn(pub, msg, sig: array of byte): int;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ed25519
verifies Ed25519 signatures (RFC 8032), in pure Limbo on
.IR keyring (2)'s
.BR IPint .
Neither this tree nor 9front's
.B libsec
implements Ed25519, so this is a from-scratch port of the twisted
Edwards curve edwards25519, in the same style as
.IR p256 (2):
field arithmetic modulo 2\u255\d\-19, points in extended homogeneous
coordinates, and point decompression by a square root modulo the
field prime. Only verification is provided \(em there is no signing.
.PP
.B Init
loads
.IR keyring (2)
and precomputes the curve constants; it returns
.B nil
on success or an error string.
.PP
.B Verify
checks a 64-byte PureEdDSA signature
.I sig
(the encoded point R followed by the scalar S) over
.I msg
under the 32-byte public key
.IR pub .
It returns 1 if the signature is valid and 0 otherwise, including for
malformed inputs (wrong lengths, a public key or R that is not a valid
curve point, or an S that is not reduced modulo the group order). The
message is taken as-is (PureEdDSA), so a caller that signs a hash
passes that hash as
.IR msg .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/crypt/ed25519.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ed25519test (1),
.IR p256 (2),
.IR ssh (2),
.IR keyring (2)
.SH BUGS
Verification only. The implementation is straightforward bigint
arithmetic on
.BR IPint ,
not constant-time, which is acceptable for public-key verification
(the inputs are public) but would not be for signing. The verification
equation is the common
.B "[S]B = R + [k]A" ,
which accepts the standard signatures OpenSSH and
.IR ssh-keygen (1)
produce; it does not apply the RFC 8032 cofactored check.
.SH HISTORY
Added to let
.IR ssh (2)
accept
.B ssh-ed25519
host keys.
